{title: Our Refuge and Our Strength}
{subtitle: Psalm 46}
{key: G}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Our God, our refuge and our strength
A help [C]so near in need
[D]We will [G]not fear though earth [C]gives way
And mountains fall to [D]sea
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Though wa[G]ters roar and foam and rage
[C]And hills [G]shake at the [C]swell
A river [D]gladdens [G]God's own town
Where [C]the Most High will dwell
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]The na[D]tions rage, the [G]kingdoms [Em]fall
He lifts His [D]voice, earth melts
Yet [C]God is in her [D]midst, she [G]stands
He helps her [C]when day breaks
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
The [G]Lord of [D]hosts is [G]here with us
Our fortress, [C]Jacob's [G]God
Be [C]still, and know that [D]I am [G]God
Let all the [C]earth be yours
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro}
